// Back: a rounded chevron.
//
// The earlier version closed its stroked path, which joined the two arms with a
// third edge and drew a hollow TRIANGLE instead of a chevron. This one is open:
// two arms meeting at a softened tip, with round ends.
//
// Vector icons have square or butt caps only, so the round ends are small
// filled circles (the stroke's own diameter) laid over the arm ends, and the tip
// is rounded by running the stroke through a short quadratic instead of a sharp
// join. Whole or half units, centred on both axes of the canvas (24: x 9..15,
// y 6..18; 16: x 6..10, y 4..12), so forward is an exact mirror and the pair
// does not splay. Keep it symmetric about the canvas centre if the size changes.
//
// FLIPS_IN_RTL: a back arrow points the other way in right-to-left locales.
//
// TWO CANVAS REPS: Chromium picks the rep matching the requested size, so the
// 16 rep is drawn at 16 rather than scaled down from 24, which is what keeps it
// crisp in the toolbar.

CANVAS_DIMENSIONS, 24,
FLIPS_IN_RTL,
STROKE, 2.f,
MOVE_TO, 15, 6,
LINE_TO, 10.4, 10.6,
QUADRATIC_TO, 9, 12, 10.4, 13.4,
LINE_TO, 15, 18,
NEW_PATH,
CIRCLE, 15, 6, 1,
NEW_PATH,
CIRCLE, 15, 18, 1,

CANVAS_DIMENSIONS, 16,
FLIPS_IN_RTL,
STROKE, 1.5f,
MOVE_TO, 10, 4,
LINE_TO, 7.1, 6.9,
QUADRATIC_TO, 6, 8, 7.1, 9.1,
LINE_TO, 10, 12,
NEW_PATH,
CIRCLE, 10, 4, 0.75f,
NEW_PATH,
CIRCLE, 10, 12, 0.75f
